{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1108028-magic-tied-to-the-spirit-world","id":1108028,"title":"Magic tied to the spirit world","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-26T08:02:06-07:00","id":1108028,"title":"Magic tied to the spirit world","content":"Is there a from of magic or witchcraft available to mortal which uses essence or is somehow tied to the Shadow/spirit world? Or is that only for spirits and werewolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T09:08:18-07:00","id":1108041,"title":"","content":"The Purified template from first edition's World of Darkness: Immortals harnesses power from the Shadow, although someone who sets out to become Purified and succeeds is no longer &quot;mortal.&quot;<br /> Wolf-Blooded in second edition Forsaken develop various supernatural Tells, some of which resemble Shadow mediumship more than anything with shapeshifting, and some of them become Wolf-Blooded in life without being part of a werewolf lineage, but simply by being moon-blessed.<br /> Hunter: the Vigil's 1e Spirit Slayers book has Les Mysteres, a conspiracy of spirit mediums who seek communion and cooperation with the Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T09:11:58-07:00","id":1108043,"title":"","content":"The most obvious route is just by getting hold of an Essence source, and just bribing spirits with it to do what you need. If you can manage to ward a Locus, and find a way to absorb Essence from it over time, then you can just feed spirits that can do what you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T09:36:30-07:00","id":1108046,"title":"","content":"There's not much in the way of mortal magic, unfortunately. A lot is implied, and it seems to be possible within the setting, considering the repetitive mentions of human occultists that clearly aren't mages, but there's not a lot of mechanics offered for it.<br /> <br /> Most of the common spirit magic would really be more like finding about a certain spirit and doing things to appease it. Certain spirits might have a ban that allow humans to take advantage. Like 'must bless a being that offers human sacrifice in the lake its bound to,' so a mortal sacrificing another in the lake would get a nice blessing for a month. You could probably look to Inferno for advice on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T10:49:31-07:00","id":1108073,"title":"","content":"Isn't there material for this in Second Sight and Book Of Spirits? Using Relics might help you as well, such as those shown <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027348-a-shaman-s-toolkit-merits-and-items-for-dealing-with-ephemeral-beings-homebrew\"><b>here</b></a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\"><b>here</b></a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T10:55:27-07:00","id":1108076,"title":"","content":"There's also the Ritual sorcery from Fall of Iseiron in the Dark Eras companion. It could easily be adapted to use spirit Essence instead of Arisen Pillars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T10:59:50-07:00","id":1108077,"title":"","content":"If memory serves, there is a cult in the Tokyo setting of Forsaken 2e that can do some spirit stuff. Otherwise, there really isn't much on magick outside of the ones provided by the various splat books. The first edition second sight book might have some information, but otherwise i'm not sure of one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T12:33:51-07:00","id":1108106,"title":"","content":"I seem to recall the core CofD having rules to create rituals to summon, ward and banish ephemerals that mortals can use. Once you know the specific rituals, its just a question of summoning a spirit in a warding space then offer its freedom for whatever effect you want to achieve. (and hope the spirit cannot comprehend the concept of vengeance or retribution :P).<br /> <br /> Edit: Yup just checked the book, it starts at page 138, in the antagonist section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":11312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","user":"Maitrecorbo","date":". 06-26-2017, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T12:40:03-07:00","id":1108109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1108028-magic-tied-to-the-spirit-world?p=1108041#post1108041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Purified template from first edition's World of Darkness: Immortals harnesses power from the Shadow, although someone who sets out to become Purified and succeeds is no longer &quot;mortal.&quot;<br /> Wolf-Blooded in second edition Forsaken develop various supernatural Tells, some of which resemble Shadow mediumship more than anything with shapeshifting, and some of them become Wolf-Blooded in life without being part of a werewolf lineage, but simply by being moon-blessed.<br /> Hunter: the Vigil's 1e Spirit Slayers book has Les Mysteres, a conspiracy of spirit mediums who seek communion and cooperation with the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gr8. Immortals is something I wanted to use. Les mysteres also sound interesting. <br /> <br /> Let me explain what I am trying to do. I wanna build an occult horror setting with the pc's being investigators (possibly low powered psychics) who investigate the spirit world and people meddling with the spirit world. The tone is dark, magic will come with a price and so does occult knowledge. Paranormal occurences are increasing and no one knows why. The setting will have:<br /> <br /> 1. Investigators/hunters<br /> 2. Spirits (duh! possibly a pantheon of some sort.)<br /> 3. Cults (probably worshipping some of the major spirits)<br /> 4. Witchcraft/sorcery (leading to corruption)<br /> 5. Anomalies (possessed/ridden, immortals, serial killers, Shadow pacts, cursed items/grimoires)<br /> 6. Conspiracies (not sure about this one yet, possibly factions working together with spirits, maybe with pacts?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T12:43:08-07:00","id":1108110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jan Paparazzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1108028-magic-tied-to-the-spirit-world?p=1108109#post1108109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me explain what I am trying to do. I wanna build an occult horror setting with the pc's being investigators (possibly low powered psychics) who investigate the spirit world and people meddling with the spirit world.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might want to check out the Illuminated Brotherhood from Spirit Slayers, the same book that has Les Mysteres.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T12:50:11-07:00","id":1108113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1108028-magic-tied-to-the-spirit-world?p=1108073#post1108073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there material for this in Second Sight and Book Of Spirits? Using Relics might help you as well, such as those shown <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1027348-a-shaman-s-toolkit-merits-and-items-for-dealing-with-ephemeral-beings-homebrew\"><b>here</b></a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\"><b>here</b></a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gr8, I think I might need second sight. Certainly for the psychics, but I think the chapter about low magic/hedge magic could be what I am looking for. And cultists... yeah I need that book. Ah, the relics could be of use and reliquery too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","ran